 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(N)$ where $N$ is the number of voxels [G].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(1)$ auxiliary memory (fixed-size buffers). The scalar field storage is $O(N)$ if stored, or $O(1)$ if computed on the fly per voxel [G].
-*   **Measured Performance:** Limited by CPU bottlenecks at high resolutions or blob counts [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Strengths:** Simple implementation, easy to debug, serves as a reference for GPU implementations [G].
-*   **Limitations:** Poor scalability due to CPU-bound field evaluation and geometry generation. High CPU-GPU transfer overhead if not batched effectively [G].
-*   **When to use:** Reference implementation, low-resolution previews, or educational purposes [G].
-*   **When not to use:** High-resolution real-time rendering, large datasets [G].
+*   **Time Complexity:** $O(N)$ where $N$ is the number of voxels. Each voxel is processed independently.
